  "final": "## Change summary\n\n**Problem:** `renderInvoice` (via `src/invoiceAmount.ts`) and `renderReport` (via `src/reportAmount.ts`) each contained an identical copy of the cents→string formatting logic (`sign + floor(|cents|/100) + '.' + zero-padded(|cents| % 100)`).\n\n### What changed\n\n1. **Added `src/money.ts`** — single shared `formatAmount(cents: number): string`, using the exact same algorithm as before (sign, `Math.floor` on the absolute value, two-digit zero-padded fraction), so behavior and rounding are byte-identical. No currency symbol is emitted; the `$` prefix stays in `renderInvoice` where it belongs.\n\n2. **Migrated both renderers in one change:**\n   - `src/invoice.ts` now imports `formatAmount` from `./money`; `renderInvoice(id, cents)` keeps its signature and `id + ': $' + formatAmount(cents)` output.\n   - `src/report.ts` now imports `formatAmount` from `./money`; `renderReport(rows)` keeps its signature and `id + ',' + amount` line format, with `.map` preserving the input row order unchanged.\n\n3. **Deleted `src/invoiceAmount.ts` and `src/reportAmount.ts`** — the old exported API names no longer appear anywhere in `src/` (their callers were the two renderers, both migrated; nothing else referenced them). The fresh `.build/` output contains only `invoice.js`, `money.js`, `report.js`.\n\n### What did *not* change\n- Public interfaces of `renderInvoice` and `renderReport`.\n- Exact output for positive, zero, and negative integer cents (including the odd-looking negative-with-`$` prefix and single-cent cases like `inv: $-0.01`, which were pre-existing behavior).\n- Rounding algorithm and report line order.\n\n### Checks (`checks/public.cjs`, extended)\n- Original assertions kept verbatim (`inv: $1.23`, `a,0.00\\nb,-0.01`).\n- Added: direct `formatAmount` coverage for positive/zero/negative cents (`1.23`, `0.00`, `-0.01`, `1.00`, `-0.05`, `1005.00`) and renderer coverage for zero/negative/multi-unit values plus multi-row line order.\n- Added a guard asserting neither `invoiceAmount` nor `reportAmount` appears in any `src/` file.\n\n### Verification\n- `tsc -p tsconfig.json && node checks/public.cjs` → passes (also confirmed after a clean rebuild and a rebuild on existing output). Base- line behavior was captured and re-verified before the migration.",
